{"id": "e0d8922452", "title": "Program runner over the task graph", "goal": "Build piece 2 of the approved a task plan, as its done lines 7 to 16 describe. create_task takes program, a plain JavaScript script whose host functions use Infinitary's own names, task() and ask(), with no promise that a Claude script runs unchanged. The runner evaluates the script in its own process and files each part as a child task. Each part's checked typed result resolves the script's await. After a quit, the runner replays the script from the task record. The program returns its branch and typed result. Bounds: before the program starts, the agent proposes an upper bound on the total number of task() calls. When that number is large, it asks the captain on a card. If a run exceeds the proposed bound, it asks on a card again.", "userWords": "Approve and build on the a task plan card (answers: animation tree, dialect own-names, consent like-a-spawn, delivery branch-and-result, check host-checks, ruling agents-reach, bounds: \"the rec, but before we start the program, the agent should propose an upperbound for how many total agent() calls can happen, and when the number is large enough, ask user via a card. and if the program exceeds the proposed upperbound, also ask user via a card\").", "parentTitle": "Dynamic workflows as programs over the task graph", "way": "plan-piece", "month": "2026-10", "tags": ["feature"]}
