{"id": "bb2f9d45a5", "title": "Keep a task open when Merge meets an open question", "goal": "Build a task's approved plan, together with a task's approved plan (read a task's report and card answers in full). From a task: crewmate instructions say to settle questions before raising a merge card. A Merge click, a first-mate close or an outside-merge close with another question or pull request open merges without closing the task, and the agent judges the next step. From a task: hold a self-merging task's story note off the captain's stack until the merge has a result, then show it once with \"Merged on its own\". When only the captain can pass a hold, the first mate sets the task to ask first and the note becomes the usual Merge card.", "userWords": "see how a task raised two cards for me at the same time? this is something to avoid, because i think right now if i click merge it will close the task and the other decision card will be gone without me having a chance to decide. we should fold this into the ongoing work around change records and merge process. ideally, open decisions should be clarified before the agent raises a merge card. but if they both got raised, then we should make sure the merge card doesn't close the task directly. rationalize this into the remaining work stream — On the plan card: prevent = words only (instructions, no refusal; drop spec items 1 and 2); fallback = keep-open; where = after PR #960. Written in: \"ok we should just avoid building rigid logic that says \"the task will then auto close after the open decision\". it should become the agent's judgment for what's the appropriate next steps\"", "parentTitle": "Let the completion card declare which merge finishes a task", "way": "asked", "month": "2026-11", "tags": ["feature", "prompts"]}
